  - sensitivity analysis
  - identifiability
abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for deterministic
  demography, resource-constrained permanent household migration,
  evidence-grounded spatial experiments, and explicit temporary mobility and
  aggregation under declared model assumptions. Version 0.3.6 preserves the
  model-semantics-v35 state produced by the completed Scientific Audit v5
  remediation programme. Audit v5 independently interrogated the immutable
  v0.3.5/model-semantics-v33 baseline across Areas A-N and demonstrated eight
  findings (4 P1 and 4 P2). All eight were repaired or explicitly dispositioned,
  and every P1 repair received independent post-merge adversarial re-verification.
  Because Audit v5 discovered new P1 findings, it is a non-clean convergence pass;
  v0.3.6 is the repaired baseline for further fresh independent auditing, not a
  claim of empirical archaeological validity or model correctness.
